  "verbalization": "Nilvadipine is shown to have a binding interaction with Cacna2d1 and Cacna2d3, which are calcium channel subunits, and these subunits are bound by Amlodipine and Isradipine, respectively. Both Amlodipine and Isradipine are known to interact with Cyp3a4, suggesting a potential pathway through these intermediaries. The lowest common ancestors of Nilvadipine and its binders (Amlodipine, Isradipine) are classified under the category of Dihydropyridine and Calcium Channel Blockers, indicating a shared pharmacological context. The scores for the interactions suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship between Nilvadipine and Cyp3a4, with varying degrees of strength across different pathways. The evidence supports a possible mechanism where Nilvadipine, through its interaction with calcium channel subunits, may influence Cyp3a4 activity, though the exact nature of this influence remains to be elucidated.",
